nodecode-cloudgpu is a rewrite of mrhy7176's mrhy7176/hermes-cloudgpu:

  https://github.com/mrhy7176/hermes-cloudgpu
  commit 8094603d776e185cfe362618d353841e6b453189
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 CloudGPU (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider profile — the `cloudgpu` id and its one wire, the
OpenAI-compatible base at https://cloudgpu.app/v1, `CLOUDGPU_API_KEY` sent as
a bearer key, the `CLOUDGPU_BASE_URL` override, the six `fallback_models` with
`deepseek-v4.1-flash` leading, and the live model list from `GET /v1/models`,
which the original leaves to Hermes to read and this cell reads from a
`/cloudgpu` command that puts the rows in `/models`. In Nodecode the profile is
a row in the models.dev catalog table, two hooks and one command. The model
ids and display names are the original's, verbatim.

Left out: the Hermes-side plumbing, which has no Nodecode counterpart and no
bearing on what a user gets — the `providers.register_provider` call, the
`ProviderProfile` dataclass fields with no reader here (`aliases`,
`signup_url`, `default_aux_model`, `auth_type`), the `requires_hermes`
declaration and the `requires_env` block that the Hermes installer read, and
the catalog-entry install advice in the README. Hermes's own live `/v1/models`
fetch is not ported as a background refresh either: Nodecode asks for the list
when the operator types `/cloudgpu`, so a start makes no request.
